  "id": "user-journey-app-onboarding",
  "name": "User journey · App onboarding",
  "description": "Synthetic user journey of a mobile app, from the first install to a subscription or a free active user. New users arrive as a steady open stream with a random gap (uniform 2 to 8 minutes) for as long as the run lasts, so the example is meant to run unlimited. Each user draws a source (50% store, 30% ad, 20% friend) and a device, and starts with sentiment 0 and no sessions. The journey combines touchpoints, a system step (the verification service) and timers: a wait for the email link, a day-1 wait and weekly waits. One day is compressed to about 20 minutes. Sessions are a counter that bounds the weekly loop at four. Chance routes model 15% giving up the email form, 10% expired links that go to support chat, 22% denying permissions (a reduced experience), 40% skipping the tour, 55% not returning after day 1 and 12% subscribing. Support chat agents, a notification service and a verification service work backstage. Every random value derives from the definition seed 20261002 and the case and step, so the same seed always gives the same run and another seed (process run --seed N) gives another one. All numbers are synthetic illustrative assumptions, not research data, a measured app or a forecast.",
